From: lavachemist <48248311+lavachemist@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8550: keep the pcieport0 label

Linux 7.3 renamed the label of sm8550's first PCIe root port from
pcieport0 to pcie0_port0. ROCKNIX's 7.2 device trees (AYN QCS8550 common,
AYANEO Pocket) still refer to &pcieport0; give the node both labels.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8550.dtsi | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8550.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8550.dtsi
index 3157436343da..d60b1570bf39 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8550.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8550.dtsi
@@ -2467,7 +2467,7 @@ opp-suspend-1 {
 				};
 			};
 
-			pcie0_port0: pcie@0 {
+			pcie0_port0: pcieport0: pcie@0 {
 				device_type = "pci";
 				reg = <0x0 0x0 0x0 0x0 0x0>;
 				bus-range = <0x01 0xff>;
